n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/assets/aaf295d69a75c976df8aaf02ee6680486c502f7ce5719b41682cdf2499cab984.png)\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(-6,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67455965-c9d3-5ae8-8b56-2a58af95df0a" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82718332-26f0-5256-9b97-5975789934c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096128} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a53226-8fd1-5a92-9a4e-00be401bb762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096129} {:answer/id #uuid "b35463bc-3503-579c-ac4a-457f6d007852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096130} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b6b91d-5f1b-52e2-85f4-50d1fa40555e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096131} {:answer/id #uuid "f95b634e-0689-591a-a129-b430e411c7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4a53226-8fd1-5a92-9a4e-00be401bb762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096129} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d73db4f-f0b5-526a-943b-b090517102ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2a124016-013d-59ab-ae8e-3e70c3dd329b" :question/math-academy-id "q-84830" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=4(y-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=0$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(0,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61861939-69d4-5b1e-a0f0-6a1b383b775b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Vertex of a Horizontal Parabola Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035d94ba-69c6-5e75-bdce-304d08379c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286542} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ec3454-462a-548e-a113-ab3669eee311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286543} {:answer/id #uuid "f3445f00-22c2-5e58-bd68-ef1d1c31e9f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286544} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8447a3-6f3a-58d7-936c-18a3ab5a0ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286545} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3ae3b8-b114-558a-baaa-9cd784bdcee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9ec3454-462a-548e-a113-ab3669eee311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286543} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb510ce2-196a-58e9-ad70-8bc8850255e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59815e55-84df-536d-a0c7-4dbdd1c2ff68" :question/math-academy-id "q-84947" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/assets/bc451fa80b0a65a817c66822571f434736c1c5c0992b64de3c5998931bba75fd.png)\n\nWhat is the vertex of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The vertex of a right-opening parabola is the left-most point of the parabola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003808/assets/7032a13b6672d8bf66ead31a54577d25bbd47640d8c3cffeedd069d57eec9338.png)\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(3,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "67455965-c9d3-5ae8-8b56-2a58af95df0a" :knowledge-point/title "Stating the Vertex of a Vertical Parabola Given Its Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "234a5e0f-fdc4-5964-b5a1-ffdfd14bea8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286549} {:answer/id #uuid "0aee08ea-b757-57c6-b88f-5aa6fcf3f4ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286550} {:answer/id #uuid "32ead7aa-d325-53e3-9d1b-604b7f3d6916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286551} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbf64f9-be3f-5ffa-95f2-32c2ba833815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286552} {:answer/id #uuid "812b6fd6-6d90-55c0-b5dc-6dec0b610e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "234a5e0f-fdc4-5964-b5a1-ffdfd14bea8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286549} :answer-field/id #uuid "c496a190-fe6a-558c-91b2-5b3e404608b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "586fe0ed-baf1-5cf1-9b94-1dfe96efb997" :question/math-academy-id "q-84966" :question/problem "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola ${x}^{2}=-\\frac{3}{2}(y-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-0)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{8})(y-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=-\\frac{3}{8}.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=0$ and $k=1.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(0,1).$"}]}
